Z||000014||4BanGinFun||10-09-2001||07:57 PM||||<BR>why the f-bodys????? not fair!!<P>to me the best looking camaros were the 3rd generation iroc-z (which i have) then they rounded then too much for the 4th gen which just doesnt look right <P>as the firebird goes i think its the best its look in years since 77 and 78 anyway. it just isnt right that GM is cuttin off pontaics peformance car. they are showing the white flag to ford! with the gp to beat the mustangs its just not right you need a firebreathing 5.7 rwd with a 6spd to make that mustang look as if its going in reverse not a 3.8 fwd auto   <P>first the fiero now the firebird whats next!?!<P><BR>||||reg||13
Z||000015||terryk||10-10-2001||12:36 AM||||Profits be dammed....<P>If you do the math, GM effectively made about $10 per car in 2000. Think about this. They are there to make money first, cars second.<P>That's the reason any car dies. If every Fiero had a waiting list, it would still be in production. Instead, every person had 10 Fiero's to choose from. I remember the Fiero's heyday well. They didn't sell. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Flamberge||10-10-2001||12:48 AM||||Your comment makes sense. I complain about the situation simply because I am jealous that the Firebird is dying like the Fiero died. But if it goes out as a car that was "past its prime" and "didn't sell well" then it will be that much easier to pick up for cheap when I want to buy a used one. Just like Fieros. <P>On a side note, the next time any of you are driving past AutoDealer Blvd (every major city has one) check out which used cars are prominently displayed... Firebirds, always. <P>- Flamberge||||reg||1
Z||000017||AutoXdbdragSE||10-10-2001||12:51 AM||||put DOHC on that pushrod v-8 and you instantly have a 450hp + monster.. i know, i autocross with guy that has a stock unmodified ZR1 corvette.. he has dyno numbers.. 445hp @ the rear wheels.. assuming 20% driveline loss.. this is a well over 500hp stock motor.. try that with pushrods..||||reg||1
Z||000018||Tonker||10-10-2001||12:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by terryk:<BR><B>Profits be dammed....<P>If you do the math, GM effectively made about $10 per car in 2000. Think about this. They are there to make money first, cars second.<P>That's the reason any car dies. If every Fiero had a waiting list, it would still be in production. Instead, every person had 10 Fiero's to choose from. I remember the Fiero's heyday well. They didn't sell. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The real question should be "Why didn't the Fiero sell?" I think it was because GM wouldn't let Pontiac make it into the car it rightfully should have been and they didn't leverage it properly in the market. It was not the car's failure, it was GM, as usual, fumbling the ball as they should have been running into the endzone for a touchdown.<P>The concept behind the Fiero was obviously good, if not visionary. Look at many the cars that came after it by GM and other companies. Saturns are based on Fiero technology. Thay're still using this technology 17 years after the Fiero's debut. The MR2 and Miata share many of the same characteristics and are still around in some incarnation. The Miata seems to be wildly popular. The Fiero had all the ingredients, despite the way it was developed, to be a great little sports car. I think the main reason that GM didn't really like it, was that it wasn't a muscle car like all of GM's other sports car offerings. It's wasn't a heavy car with massive power, it was a small, light car with modest power and great performance. GM didn't market the car properly, it didn't develop it properly. The Fiero didn't lose GM any money. GM lost GM money.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000019||MinnGreenGT||10-10-2001||01:59 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tonker:<BR><B> It was not the car's failure, it was GM, as usual, fumbling the ball as they should have been running into the endzone for a touchdown.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Wow!  That sounds just like Denny Green and the Vikings... yet he's still the damn coach!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> What is this world coming to?||||reg||1
